{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1410005-scion-homebrew-mysteries-of-the-otherworld-expansion-ii-for-the-t\u00faatha-d\u00e9","id":1410005,"title":"Scion Homebrew - Mysteries of the Otherworld: Expansion II for the T\u00faatha D\u00e9","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-23T21:00:28-07:00","id":1410005,"title":"Scion Homebrew - Mysteries of the Otherworld: Expansion II for the T\u00faatha D\u00e9","content":"Hello everyone!<br /> <br /> I hope you are still enjoying <b>Mysteries of the World: Scion Companion </b>(and I hope you have enjoyed my alternative version of the Nemetondevos)! Just as I said last week, I wasn't actually finished posting Homebrew using the new material found in the book. So! Here is <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Mysteries of the Otherworld</b></a>, an expanded collection of rules and systems for the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann, as well as potentially other Pantheon, using the new systems.<br /> <br /> This was actually one of my favorite projects that I have gotten the chance to work on, purely because I absolutely love the new Specalized Purview mechanics with a tiny tweak from me because, I mean, I can't help myself from tweaking the game. But! Within it you can find rules to continue to expand your Scion of the T\u00faatha D\u00e9's weird niche talents, giving them the same strange relationships with humanity as the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 themselves, and finding ways to bring about their greatest war magics to your aid in your strive to be the Best and Greatest of whatever profession you have taken for yourself. In <b>Mysteries of the Otherworld</b> you can find:<ul><li>New Cult systems, including an alternative for the Light and Shadow system, since the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann have borderline no ability to be subtle as Shadow suggests, but is happy to indulge in endemic violence in a way that Light normally can't accommodate. You can also find seven new Cult Tags to help you represent the unique sorts of Cults the Pantheon of Ireland brings to play, Professional Organizations, Foster-Families, and Warrior Bands which are three alternative Foundings for Cults.</li> <li>Tweaked Covenant mechanics, allowing you Scion to play as a Professional Master, guiding mortal members of the profession through your overwhelming skill and dictating traditions, or for Soverignty Goddesses who take mortal rulers as their partners, exerting control and influencing the mortal world through them.</li> <li>Eight new Specalized Purviews, each with a unique Innate, and 3 - 4 Boons. These include:<ul><li><b>Corpses (Death)</b>: For the Corpse-Kings and Eye-Eaters and all your needs to be like The Badb herself. Build ramparts of corpses and leave countless dead at the hands of your Band to send a message.</li> <li><b>Cupbearing (Water)</b>: For those who want to wield the same power as the nine cupbearers of Nuadu, bringing a deadly thirst on enemies, and force valuable targets to leave their bastions to pick them off.</li> <li><b>Debility (Health)</b>: Wield the dire war-magics of the T\u00faatha D\u00e9, inflicting the pain of childbirth or menstruation on rival armies and rip the strength from an enemy's muscles.</li> <li><b>Frenzy (Chaos</b><b>)</b>: Scream to the sky with Nemain and leave the world around you a confused mess of violence, force people to take violent actions, and drive your enemies and allies into senseless rages.</li> <li><b>Raiding (War)</b>: Take what you want from your enemies, enriching yourself through martial exploits, placing your enemies under tithes to strip them of their wealth even as they earn it, and lead your allies in lightning quick raids while preventing even the loudest thunderer from giving your ambush away.</li> <li><b>R\u00edge (Order)</b>: Walk in the footsteps of Conare M\u00f3r and bring overwhelming peace and natural beauty to your lands, forcing even the natural world to bend against your supreme kingship, and force even the most violent outbreak into negotiation.</li> <li><b>Shame (Artistry, Passion)</b>: For the most dire satirists and <i>f\u00edli</i>, Scions who wield the grim powers of satire against their enemies to cause explosions of boils that kill and strip even the greatest king of their authority through ridicule.</li> <li><b>Soverignty (Fertility, Order)</b>: For the Soverignty figures who reward good kingship with abundance and take on the form of horrific cannibalistic hags when wronged.</li> </ul></li> </ul>As ever, if you have any questions and comments, feel free to shout here or in the Scion fan Discord. I hope everyone is enjoying themselves with the new books and are excited to see what is coming next for Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T13:04:56-07:00","id":1410116,"title":"","content":"Watcher,you are clearly not even in the general vicinity of fucking around.<br /> <br /> jokes aside,thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T15:22:52-07:00","id":1410141,"title":"","content":"I see something made by Watcher, I go get it. Simple as that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24323-zipdrive","name":"ZipDrive","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T07:00:05-07:00","id":1410282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZipDrive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main